our]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 1½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cream of Tartar|cream of tartar]] (or baking powder)\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Buttermilk|buttermilk]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Eggs|eggs]], separated\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] (optional)\n* 1 cup frozen [[Cookbook:Blueberry|blueberries]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Sift together flour, sugar, baking powder, cream of tartar, salt, cinnamon and nutmeg. Set aside.\n# Whisk together buttermilk, butter and egg yolks in a large bowl. Mix flour mixture into buttermilk mixture. Mix in blueberries.\n# [[Cookbook:Whipping|Whip]] egg whites in a small bowl until stiff, but do not let dry peaks form. Fold into pancake batter.\n# Heat a large pan or [[Cookbook:Griddle|griddle]] over medium heat. Lightly spray or [[Cookbook:Brush|brush]] with vegetable oil.  Ladle in a ¼ cup of batter for each pancake; cook until set and bubbly on the top. Turn pancake over, then cook for 1 more minute.\n# Serve warm with whatever topping you prefer.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for pancakes]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using blueberry]]\n[[Category:Breakfast recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using buttermilk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cooking spray]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream of tartar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Blueberry Pancakes","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1¾ cup all-purpose flour","sourceText":"1¾ cup all-purpose flour","amountText":"